  "description": "NOPMOX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: 0.44(C56 H132 Eu6 N12 O25),0.56(C56 H132 N12 O25 Tb6),4(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb1A (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb2A (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb3A (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Eu1? (Eu) has 0 O neighbors; Eu2? (Eu) has 0 O neighbors; Eu3? (Eu) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 4 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.560-5.176 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.33-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (Eu,Tb)6(OH)8O(piv)8(deta)4·4CH3CN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
